!!id:"https://tson.io/test-suite/class2/schema/invalid/a-sibling-reference-as-an-explicit-application-argument-expected.tn"
!!import:"https://tson.io/test-suite/schemas/schema-sidecar.tn"
{
  spec: "[TSON-SCHEMA] §5.2, [TSON-SCHEMA] §8.1"
  description: """
    The reference atom reads a sibling reference wherever a reference stands, and the position rule refuses it at
    every slot but a record field's type, naming the slot. `record_field.type` admits one only as the whole reference:
    an argument of an application is a template argument, so `box< kind! >` is refused even at a field's type, and
    even though `cell` declares `kind`.
    """
  error: {
    category: resolver
  }
}
